---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const faqSchema = {
 "@context": "https://schema.org",
 "@type": "FAQPage",
 "mainEntity": [
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Which ports must be open for a website?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Inbound 80 and 443 on the web server; everything else can stay closed. Management ports (22/3389) should be restricted to known IPs."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Does closing ports improve security?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Reducing the exposed surface always helps, but hardening the services behind open ports matters more."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "How do I check open ports?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "From outside: an online port scanner against your address. From the server: ss -tlnp or netstat -tlnp."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "What is port forwarding?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Telling a NAT router to send inbound traffic on one port to a specific internal device: the workaround for hosting behind NAT."
   }
  }
 ]
}
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Common Network Ports: The Reference List | PromptDNS"
  description="The common network ports reference: web, mail, DNS, remote access, and database ports with what each protocol does and safe defaults."
  schema={[faqSchema]}
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-12">
    <nav class="mb-4 text-sm text-ink-faint" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/" class="hover:text-accent">Home</a>
       <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <a href="/ip-and-networking/" class="hover:text-accent">IP & Networking</a>
       <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <span class="text-ink-dim">Common Network Ports</span>
    </nav>
    <h1 class="font-display text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-4xl">Common Network Ports</h1>
    <p class="mt-5 text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Ports are numbered doors on a machine: the port in a connection decides which program answers. Firewalls and servers live and die by getting this list right.</p>
    <div class="rich-text mt-8">
      <h2 class="font-display mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-ink">The ports that matter</h2>
      <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60"><table class="pdns-table"><thead><tr><th></th><th></th><th></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">80</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">HTTP</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">Web, unencrypted (redirects to HTTPS)</td></tr><tr><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">443</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">HTTPS</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">Web, encrypted: the modern default</td></tr><tr><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">53</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">DNS</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">Queries (UDP) and zone transfers (TCP)</td></tr><tr><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">25</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">SMTP</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">Server-to-server mail relay</td></tr><tr><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">587</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">SMTP submission</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">User outgoing mail with STARTTLS</td></tr><tr><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">465</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">SMTPS</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">User outgoing mail, implicit TLS</td></tr><tr><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">993</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">IMAPS</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">Receiving mail, encrypted</td></tr><tr><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">995</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">POP3S</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">Receiving mail (POP), encrypted</td></tr><tr><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">22</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">SSH</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">Remote server administration</td></tr><tr><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">3389</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">RDP</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">Windows remote desktop</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
      <h2 class="font-display mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Well-known vs ephemeral</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-5"><li class="leading-relaxed">0-1023 are well-known ports reserved for core services; servers listen there.</li><li class="leading-relaxed">49152-65535 are ephemeral: your browser picks a random one as the source port for each connection.</li><li class="leading-relaxed">Firewalls block inbound on ephemeral ranges by default; that is correct and normal.</li></ul>
      <h2 class="font-display mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Frequently asked questions</h2>
      <div class="mt-3 grid gap-3"><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">Which ports must be open for a website?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Inbound 80 and 443 on the web server; everything else can stay closed. Management ports (22/3389) should be restricted to known IPs.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">Does closing ports improve security?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Reducing the exposed surface always helps, but hardening the services behind open ports matters more.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">How do I check open ports?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">From outside: an online port scanner against your address. From the server: ss -tlnp or netstat -tlnp.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">What is port forwarding?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Telling a NAT router to send inbound traffic on one port to a specific internal device: the workaround for hosting behind NAT.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">How do I verify my changes?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Run the record lookup to confirm live values, then check the propagation checker for worldwide agreement. Both tools run in your browser.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">What TTL should I use?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">3600 seconds is the default. Drop to 300 a day before changes so cutover is quick, then restore.</p></details></div>
      <h2 class="font-display mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Related</h2>
      <ul class="mt-3 grid gap-2"><li><a href="/what-is-ssl-tls/" class="text-accent hover:text-accent-soft">DNS port numbers →</a></li><li><a href="/smtp-tester/" class="text-accent hover:text-accent-soft">SMTP preflight →</a></li><li><a href="/smtp-tester/" class="text-accent hover:text-accent-soft">Email ports guide →</a></li></ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
